#   row of the window, then indexer_shard.prompt_shard scored only this rank's ceil(R / world) rows
#   (sparse._prompt_rank_pools reads qi[lo:hi] alone) and all-gathered the pools. Two thirds of that projection, at
#   every DSA layer of every chunk with sparse rows, was never read at three ranks.
# - indexer_shard.prompt_rows(R, rank, world): the rows a rank scores, one owner of the fact; prompt_shard and
#   dsa_rows both take it.
# - forward.dsa_rows: the projection on prompt_rows' rows when the sharded selection runs, every row otherwise
#   (select_tokens, decode windows, TF_GLM_KV_SHARD's own path untouched).
#
